id: S22
target: src/sello/scalar.nim
desc: geScalarmultCT: runtime [1P..8P] table-build step selects the wrong cached operand, 'geAdd(step0, pts[i - 1], table[0])' -> 'geAdd(step0, pts[i - 1], table[i - 1])' -- doubles pts[i-1] against itself instead of adding P via table[0], so the table holds powers of two times P (P, 2P, 4P, 8P, 16P, ...) instead of consecutive multiples (P, 2P, 3P, ..., 8P), corrupting every digit lookup downstream. RFC-004 slice 8b's "table-select index flip" target.
====OLD====
    geAdd(step0, pts[i - 1], table[0])
====NEW====
    geAdd(step0, pts[i - 1], table[i - 1])
====END====
